      "label": "Figure 8",
      "kind": "figure",
      "number": "8",
      "page": 20,
      "caption": "lists the 3 highest-scored and the 3 lowest-scored shapes of CAW, which are extracted from the Wikipedia dataset with M = 32 and m = 3. A law of general motif closure can be observed from the highest-scored CAWs: two nodes that commonly appear in some types of motif are more inclined to have a link in between. For example, the highest-scored shape of CAW, (0, ∞) →(1, 2) →(2, 3) →(1, 2), implies that the nodes except the ﬁrst in this CAW appear in the sampled common 3-hop neighborhood around the two nodes between which the link is to be",
